        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing, and one answer has to be chosen. Choose the answer the documents support better.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Osgood?\n\nAnswer A: 1,624\n  about: Osgood\n  sense: 2010 census\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The population was 1,624 at the 2010 census.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 2,500\n  about: Osgood\n  sense: 2010 census\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: U.S. Decennial Census\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"2010 census As of the census of 2010, there were 2,500 people, 638 households, and 417 families living in the town.\" [document 2]\n\nAnswer C: 5,000\n  about: Osgood\n  sense: 2010 census (the document does not state it)\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"There were 5,000 people, 638 households, and 417 families living in the town.\" [document 3]\n\nAnswer D: 48\n  about: Osgood\n  sense: 2010 census (the document does not state it)\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: United States Census Bureau\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"According to the United States Census Bureau, the village has a total area of , all land. As of the census of 2010, there were 48 people, 19 households, and 11 families residing in the village.\" [document 4]\n\nThe documents:\nDocument 1: Osgood, Indiana Osgood is a town in Center Township, Ripley County, in the U.S. state of Indiana. The population was 1,624 at the 2010 census. Osgood was platted in 1854 when the railroad was extended to that point. The town was named for A. L. Osgood, a railroad official. A post office called Osgood has been in operation since 1855. In 1999, the community received a $23 million bequest from the Gilmore and Golda Reynolds Foundation, which was established by two lifelong Osgood residents to assist the town government as well as local non-profit organizations. Osgood is located at (39.129062,\nDocument 2: 1960 1,434 16.8 %  \n1970 1,346 −6.1 %  \n1980 1,554 15.5 %  \n1990 1,688 8.6 %  \n2000 1,669 −1.1 %  \n2010 2,500 49.9 %  \n2020 2,450 −2.0 %  \nU.S. Decennial Census  \n2010 census  \nAs of the census of 2010, there were 2,500 people, 638 households, and 417 families living in the town. The population density was 1,720.0 inhabitants per square mile (664.1/km²). There were 728 housing units at an average density of 502.1 per square mile (193.9/km²). The racial makeup of the town was 98.2% White,...\nDocument 3: There were 5,000 people, 638 households, and 417 families living in the town. The population density was 1,120.0 inhabitants per square mile (432.4/km²). There were 728 housing units at an average density of 502.1 per square mile (193.9/km²). The racial makeup of the town was 98.2% White, 0.1% African American, 0.2% Native American, 0.1% from other races, and 1.5% from two or more races. Hispanic or Latino of any race were 1.3% of the population. There were 638 households.\nDocument 4: Osgood, Missouri Osgood is a village in Sullivan County, Missouri, United States. The population was 48 at the 2010 census. Osgood was platted in 1886. and most likely named after a railroad man. A post office called Osgood was established in 1888, and remained in operation until 1965. Osgood is located at (40.199175, -93.348822). According to the United States Census Bureau, the village has a total area of , all land. As of the census of 2010, there were 48 people, 19 households, and 11 families residing in the village. The population density was . There were 31 housing units\nDocument 6: . 2000 census [ edit ] As of the census [ 3 ] of 2000 , there were 255 people , 103 households , and 77 families living in the village . The population density was 742.1 inhabitants per square mile ( 286.5/km 2 ) . There were 104 housing units at an average density of 302.7 per square mile ( 116.9/km 2 ) . The racial makeup of the village was 100.00 % White . There were 103 households , out of which 25.2 % had children under the age of 18 living with them , 64.1 % were\n\nWeigh the evidence. Which documents are specific, and consistent within themselves: do their names, dates and other details fit together? Which fit what the other documents say? Does any document read as altered, or out of place? Judge by the documents alone.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one or two sentences\", \"choice\": \"A\"}"
